  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 121 PM CDT Wed Sep 23 2026\n\nSaturday through Wednesday:\n\nThe extended models have fairly good agreement with the overall\npattern this weekend into next week. An upper ridge will \nprevail over the wrn Great Lakes through Mon, although a weak \nshortwave trough will attempt to run through the ridge late Sun \nafternoon into Mon AM. Dry low to mid level air will likely hold\nand no precipitation is forecast at this time. \n\nFinally, an organized upper trough will move into the Great \nPlains Mon nt-Tue and with some degree of cyclogenesis \nexpected. A swly low level jet will bring a return of higher \nmoisture content air followed by a cold front late Tue nt or Wed\nAM. Showers are likely (60-70 percent chance) along with a \nslight chance of thunderstorms for Tue nt, lingering into Wed. \nHigh temps may return to the lower 70s early next week before \nthe cold front arrives. \n\nGehring",
